1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,200
Every book starts as a thought worth saving.

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:08,067
Book Genesis Five helps you turn that thought
into a working manuscript.

3
00:00:08,067 --> 00:00:10,800
Install with Python three point ten or newer,

4
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:14,600
and connect the model route you already use.

5
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:17,100
Run Book Genesis new.

6
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:21,433
Add one sentence for your idea,
and choose the language.

7
00:00:21,433 --> 00:00:24,500
Review the brief, outline, and first chapter.

8
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:28,000
Press Enter to continue, or type a note
to steer the work.

9
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,800
Quit and resume whenever you need.

10
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:36,000
Your drafts and revision history
stay on your machine.

11
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:42,133
Open the local reader, move between chapters,
and compare versions.

12
00:00:42,133 --> 00:00:45,400
Export your working manuscript
as Markdown or EPUB.

13
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:49,700
Incomplete projects are labeled as partial.

14
00:00:49,700 --> 00:00:52,300
Book Genesis Five. Open source beta.

15
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:55,000
Creativity comes first.

16
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,900
Your story. Your choices.
